{title: Scarborough Fair}
{artist: Traditional}
{key: Am}

{c: Verse 1}
Are you [Am]going to [G]Scarborough [Am]Fair?
[C]Parsley, [G]sage, rose[Am]mary and [Am]thyme.
Re[Am]member [G]me to one who lives [C]there,
For [Am]once she [G]was a true love of [Am]mine.

{c: Verse 2}
Tell her to [Am]make me a [G]cambric [Am]shirt,
[C]Parsley, [G]sage, rose[Am]mary and [Am]thyme.
With[Am]out no [G]seam nor needle[C]work,
Then [Am]she'll be a [G]true love of [Am]mine.
